{"name":"Liver","hex":"#654a46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Liver","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["From or pertaining to Liverpool."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Liver"}],"entries":[{"title":"Liver","blocks":[{"text":"The liver is a major metabolic organ exclusively found in vertebrates which performs many essential biological functions, such as detoxification of the organism and the synthesis of various proteins and other biochemicals necessary for digestion and growth. In humans, it is located in the right upper quadrant of the abdomen, below the diaphragm and mostly shielded by the lower right rib cage. Its other metabolic roles include carbohydrate metabolism, the production of a number of hormones, conversion and storage of nutrients such as glucose and glycogen, and the decomposition of red blood cells. Anatomical and medical terminology often use the prefix hepat- from ἡπατο-, from the Greek word for liver, such as hepatology, and hepatitis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Anatomy_Abdomen_Tiesworks.jpg/330px-Anatomy_Abdomen_Tiesworks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liver","wikidata":"Q9368"},{"title":"Liver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Liver is a color name for a kind of brown, first recorded as such in English in 1686. It may refer to the color of the organ."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liver_(color)","wikidata":"Q536284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Liver_01_animation1.gif/330px-Liver_01_animation1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Liver_01_animation1.gif/330px-Liver_01_animation1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiv